      sources: "Sources: examples/non-person-identity (tests and fixtures, fictional). Chapter 06, “Lab 1: fixtures, no tenant,” steps 1–3.",
      say: `Lab 1 needs only a laptop, PowerShell 7 and Pester, plus the runs of Chapters 1, 2 and 3: the register, the owners and the owners' decisions. First you run Learn's own procedures against the stand-ins, and you can read the test where the migration-state step fails, just as it would on a real server. Then you list what each task is allowed to run: the read task is only lookups. Then you run the check against a fictional estate. Nine accounts are in scope, with six findings and five planned writes: four for the pipeline to send and one for a person. And the hand-off isn't ready yet. Let's see why.`,
      detail: `You need PowerShell 7.1 or later with Pester 5. Work in examples/non-person-identity. First make the runs this chapter reads: Chapter 01's out/inventory, Chapter 02's out/ownership and Chapter 03's out/matrix, with the commands of Chapter 03's Lab 1, step 3 (./Invoke-NpiInventory.ps1, ./Invoke-NpiOwnership.ps1 and ./Invoke-NpiMatrix.ps1, each piped to Out-Null). It prints nothing. The three folders hold the register, the owners and the owners' D-NP3 decisions this chapter reads. Step 1, run Learn's procedures against the stand-ins: Invoke-Pester -Path tests/KerberosIslandSamples.Tests.ps1 -Output None -PassThru | Select-Object PassedCount, FailedCount, NotRunCount gives PassedCount 17, FailedCount 0, NotRunCount 0. Read the test for the state-3 step: Learn's block fails with "A parameter cannot be found that matches parameter name 'Properties'". Step 2, list what each task runs: kerberos-island: Get-ADComputer, Get-ADDomainController, Get-ADObject, Get-ADServiceAccount, Get-ADUser. kerberos-apply: Complete-ADServiceAccountMigration, Disable-ADAccount, Get-ADComputer, Get-ADDomainController, Get-ADObject, Get-ADServiceAccount, Get-ADUser, Move-ADObject, New-ADServiceAccount, Set-ADServiceAccount, Start-ADServiceAccountMigration. Step 3, check the Kerberos accounts and build the plan: ./Invoke-NpiKerberosIsland.ps1 -Cloud gcc -RegisterRun out/inventory -MatrixRun out/matrix -ProgramDatesPath tests/fixtures/ch03/inputs/program-dates.json -FixturePath tests/fixtures/estate.json -KerberosFixturePath tests/fixtures/ch06/ad-kerberos.json -InputPath tests/fixtures/ch06/inputs -OutputPath out/kerberos. Output: Kerberos accounts: 9 in scope; KDS root key Ready. Findings: 6 Finding, 1 Warn, 2 Info. Plan: 10 actions, 5 of them writes (1 CompleteDmsaMigration, 2 CreateGmsa, 2 SetRetrievers); nothing sent. Run by: 1 person, 4 pipeline. Island list: 6 accounts, 4 ready for P4.6; hand-off ready: False. Reconciliation (D11 KerberosIsland): 1 HandedOff, 4 OnIslandList, 1 Unreconciled. Plan SHA-256: 4021225078c239e5c842fc3f0563222cff13b2099a33ca088cdc026601b8268f. The plan's hash is the same on every run with these inputs. Run by counts the writes by who sends them: four are the pipeline's, one a person's. The commands run Learn's pinned procedures against stand-ins, and run the example against a fictional estate and a fake Active Directory; -Apply in Lab 1 changes only the fake, in memory.`,
